A||N||7||kornholio||cleaning throttle body||||1||
Z||000000||kornholio||12-04-1999||03:47 PM||||I bought a can of throttle body cleaner today and it says to spray it into the throttle body while the engine is running.  I did this and the engine wanted to stall.  I stopped spraying as soon as it started stumbling.  Is it supposed to do this?  If I open the butterfly valve while spraying, will it stop it from stalling?  Also, is there any damage from this cleaner stuff going into the engine?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||12-04-1999||05:32 PM||||It's normal for the engine to stumble and try to stall when you spray cleaner into it. You can try opening the throttle a little, but it will still run very rough until it clears out.  I have used throttle body cleaners for years and have not had any ill effects to the engine.  The stuff is designed to pass through and be burned in the cylinders.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Trixi||12-05-1999||11:31 PM||||Be careful not to use it too much<BR>I had a problem with using too much,<BR>i had to replace rings because of it||||reg||11
Z||000003||Patrick||12-05-1999||11:34 PM||||<BR>Trixi, you weren't spraying too much of that stuff around your transmission recently were you? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000004||Carrolles||12-06-1999||06:40 AM||||Spray some on a rag and wipe away as much carbon buildup as you can prior to spraying it while the engine is running.  Get behind the butterfly also.<P>I've used the B&G decarbonizing kit and it worked great.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AL||12-06-1999||09:13 PM||||HEY CORN TRY BRAKE CLEANER THAT STUFF CLEANS IT VERY GOOD AND IT DRYS FAST, SPRAY IT IN WITH THE CAR OFF.||||reg||14
Z||000006||kornholio||12-06-1999||09:21 PM||||I cleaned the throttle body and I think it has really helped with my hesitation problem.  It only hesitated once in the last 2 days.  My idle is smoother too.  Thanks for the replys.||||reg||14
Z||000007||DJRice||12-07-1999||09:27 AM||||I am working on V6 out of another Fiero now, and would like to clean the Throttle Body on it.  Will it hurt anything if I just soak it in brake parts cleaner?  I intend to remove the TPS and IAC.  The car has been sitting for quite a while, but started right up after I replaced the pickup coil (any bypassed the neutral start switch).  I dropped the engine anyway because it needs alot of TLC.<P>Its really amazing, but this is the second V6 car Ive gotten that the previous owners had left the original forward 3 spark plugs in, and had only replaced the 3 that are on the trunk side.  The Clutch Slave mount and shifter cable brackets were both broken and rigged like a champ. <P>The car needs some TLC, but its an 85 SE with <BR>PW, PDL, Trunk Release, Cruise, Sunroof, and will have Rally Gauge Kit by the time I get finshed. ||||reg||1
